                <pb facs="0290" n="206" sameAs="frus:frus1903/pg206"/>

                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Beaupré to Mr. Hay.</hi></head>
                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Telegram.]</seg></opener>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >United States Legatinon</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Bogotá</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1903-10-10"><hi rendition="#italic">October 10, 1903</hi></date>.
                        (Received October 14, 2.59 p.m.)</dateline></opener>
                <p>October 10, 1 p.m. Presentation of the committee report postponed until 12th. My
                    telegram of September 30 states the first two clauses of the report. The third
                    and last presents a project for law approving extension in time granted canal
                    company. Apparently this is proposed with the expectation that the Senate will
                    negative the project and annul extension, thus accomplishing the object stated
                    in my telegram, 9th. However, I think in case most of them vote, extension in
                    time to the company will be annulled. The probability is that Congress will
                    adjourn without taking conclusive action on this report.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Beaupré.</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
